---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import FormSlot from '../../components/FormSlot.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../../data/sites.mjs';
import { BRAND, LEGAL_POSITIONING } from '../../data/brand.mjs';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema.mjs';

const site = currentSite();
---

<Base
  title={`About ${BRAND.name} | A principal buyer of data center land`}
  description="We buy and option rural land for data center development using our own capital. We are not a brokerage and we do not represent sellers. Here is who we are and how to reach us."
  path="/about"
  schemas={[
    breadcrumbSchema(site, [
      { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { label: 'About', path: '/about' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <div class="page section">
    <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
    <h1 class="measure">Who we are</h1>

    <div class="measure stack">
      <p class="lede">
        {BRAND.name} acquires and develops rural land for data center use. We
        look for property that can support the power, space, and access these
        facilities need, and when we find it we buy the land or we take an
        option on it.
      </p>

      <p>
        We are principals. The money we put into a property is ours, and we
        carry the risk of whether a site works out. That is a meaningful
        difference from the people who normally contact landowners about their
        property, and it changes the conversation. We have no reason to talk you
        into anything, because we are the ones who have to live with the
        purchase.
      </p>

      <!--
        Required verbatim. Also rendered in the footer of every page.
        scripts/lint-copy.mjs asserts both. Do not reword.
      -->
      <p class="callout">{LEGAL_POSITIONING}</p>

      <p>
        What that means for you in practice: we do not take a commission, we do
        not advertise your land to anyone else, and there is no fee of any kind
        for talking to us. If your property does not fit what we need, we do not
        earn anything by pretending otherwise, so we will simply tell you.
      </p>

      <h2>How we evaluate property</h2>
      <p>
        We start with public records. Transmission and substation data, road
        networks, floodplain maps, and terrain tell us most of what we need to
        know before anyone visits. That work is ours, not yours. You will never
        be asked to pay for a survey or an engineering study in order to have a
        conversation with us.
      </p>

      <h2>How to reach us</h2>
      <p>
        Email is the fastest way to reach a person here.
        <a href={`mailto:${BRAND.email}`}>{BRAND.email}</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also use the form below. It reaches the same place, and it gives
        us enough to start looking at your property before we reply.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page section--tight">
    <div class="form-wrap">
      <FormSlot heading="Tell us about your land" />
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .callout {
    padding: var(--s4) var(--s5);
    background: var(--accent-tint);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .form-wrap {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
</style>
